    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27880" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mănĭfestārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		manifestus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>palpable, plain, clear, evident, manifest</i>
			(ante- and post-class. for manifestus): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Aul. 3, 4, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moechus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Bacch. 4, 8, 77</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">teneo hunc manifestarium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Trin. 4, 2, 50</span></i>
			.—Of things: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Mil. 2, 5, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">soloecismus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					1, 7, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
